    "Simplify: √75::5√3|3√5|25√3|10√3": "Break 75 into a perfect square times a leftover factor: 75 is 25 times 3, and the square root of 25 is 5. So the square root of 75 simplifies to 5 times the square root of 3.",
    "Simplify: √90::3√10|10√3|9√10|6√10": "Break 90 into a perfect square times a leftover factor: 90 is 9 times 10, and the square root of 9 is 3. So the square root of 90 simplifies to 3 times the square root of 10.",
    "Simplify: √128::8√2|2√8|64√2|16√2": "Break 128 into a perfect square times a leftover factor: 128 is 64 times 2, and the square root of 64 is 8. So the square root of 128 simplifies to 8 times the square root of 2.",
    "Simplify: √112::4√7|7√4|16√7|8√7": "Break 112 into a perfect square times a leftover factor: 112 is 16 times 7, and the square root of 16 is 4. So the square root of 112 simplifies to 4 times the square root of 7.",
