    "A triangle has two angles measuring 39° each. What is the measure of the third angle?::102°|78°|112°|141°": "Every triangle's angles add up to 180 degrees. Subtract the two you know from 180: 180 minus 39 minus 39 is 102 degrees.",
    "A right triangle has legs of length 8 and 15. What is the length of the hypotenuse?::17|23|120|19": "The Pythagorean theorem says leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. 8 squared is 64 and 15 squared is 225 — add those to get 289. The square root of 289 is 17, so that's the hypotenuse.",
    "A right triangle has a hypotenuse of 20 and one leg of 12. What is the length of the other leg?::16|8|32|14": "Use the Pythagorean theorem, leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. The known leg squared is 144, and the hypotenuse squared is 400. Subtract to isolate the missing leg: 400 minus 144 is 256. The square root of 256 is 16, so that's the other leg.",
    "Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. If one angle measures 105°, what does its alternate interior angle measure?::75°|105°|85°|15°": "Alternate interior angles formed when a transversal crosses parallel lines are always congruent — equal — to each other, so this angle also measures 105 degrees.",
