    "A right triangle has legs of length 10 and 24. What is the length of the hypotenuse?::26|34|240|28": "The Pythagorean theorem says leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. 10 squared is 100 and 24 squared is 576 — add those to get 676. The square root of 676 is 26, so that's the hypotenuse.",
