    "Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. If one same-side interior angle measures 132°, what does the other same-side interior angle measure?::48°|132°|180°|58°": "Same-side interior angles formed by a transversal crossing parallel lines are supplementary — they add up to 180 degrees. Subtract the one you know from 180: 180 minus 132 is 48 degrees.",
    "In an isosceles triangle, the two base angles are equal, and the vertex angle is 88°. What does each base angle measure?::46°|44°|92°|52°": "The two base angles of an isosceles triangle are equal, and all three angles add up to 180. Subtract the vertex angle first: 180 minus 88 is 92. Split that evenly between the two equal base angles: 92 divided by 2 is 46 degrees each.",
    "Angle A and Angle B are complementary. If Angle A is 5 times Angle B, what is Angle B?::15°|18°|30°|75°": "Complementary angles add up to 90 degrees. Since A is 5 times B, replace A with 5B: 5B plus B is 6B, and that has to equal 90. Divide 90 by 6, and B is 15 degrees.",
