    "s2::According to Figure 1, at how many of the seven measured temperatures was the reaction rate above 20 μmol/min?::1|2|3|4": "Only three temperatures clear 20 micromoles per minute: 30°C (28), 40°C (40), and 50°C (32).",
    "s2::According to Figure 1, what is the lowest reaction rate recorded, and at what temperature does it occur?::5 μmol/min at 10°C|6 μmol/min at 70°C|15 μmol/min at 20°C|18 μmol/min at 60°C": "The lowest rate on the whole figure is 5 micromoles per minute, right at the coldest temperature tested, 10°C.",
    "s2::According to Figure 1, how many different temperatures were tested in this experiment?::5|6|7|8": "Seven temperatures were tested in all: 10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, and 70°C.",
