    "A fair coin is flipped 3 times. What is the probability of getting heads all 3 times?::1/8|1/3|3/8|1/6": "Each flip doesn't affect the others, so multiply the individual probabilities together: one-half, raised to the 3rd power, since there are 3 flips. That works out to 1 over 8.",
