    "A fair coin is flipped 4 times. What is the probability of getting heads all 4 times?::1/16|1/4|4/16|1/8": "Each flip doesn't affect the others, so multiply the individual probabilities together: one-half, raised to the 4th power, since there are 4 flips. That works out to 1 over 16.",
